:: Narrative4AMDorm {"position":"275,1175","size":"100,100"}
Olive and I were high, elevating up to Saturn and then crash landing back down to New Jersey when it was over. Our confuzzled feelings were mixed  with alcohol more than the edibles we used at that time. I think I even puked a little in my mouth before we jumped into the bed. I did have two shots of that Chinese wine he gave me and then he finished it off. 

Sometimes this little love scene with Olive comes into my mind at night. Although, rarely these days, but with entering his world again. It feels raw and new.

I recall this happened after our big conversation where we exchanged these feelings under the college bleachers like some damn White people sitcom. It was Olive's plan by the way. 

There is more to this story. There was a red flag or two and I shouldn't have pulled my pants down there. We were just so desperate in our honesty [[I guess.->NarrativeTheBleachers]]


:: NarrativeChildHoodMemory1 {"position":"875,825","size":"100,100"}
I think I remember that one day, that blog post really brings back some memories. I've known Olive for so long but when we hit our puberty years I stopped knowing him. It's hard to explain and to be quite frank he never wanted to explain it me either.

When we got lost in Kids R' Fun, his dad really did slap the shit out of him. It was over something so ridiculous too. Olive and I were at the arcade playing Tekken 3.

He was Hwoarang and I was Lei Wulong. The strobing lights, the muffled SFXs, my hands sweating on the handsticks, and the dried tears on Olive's cheeks from all the hysterical laughing he was doing. I do not remember what was funny during that time, but sometimes he would break down cry laughing for simply being around me. [[>>->NarrativeChildHoodMemory2]]


:: NarrativeChildHoodMemory2 {"position":"1000,825","size":"100,100"}
"Fengfeeenng!" I heard his father call out and I turned and saw his thin figure in the dark, lightened only by the flickers of various arcade games. He was still wearing a fleece even though it was dead in the middle of a hot August.

It only took a minute after him and I locked eyes. His, totally cocked with rage, mine with total doe-eyed child fright. In that 5 seconds, I had realized that we weren't allowed here and Olive never told me that we weren't allowed there.

"Fengfeeenng!" I heard him say again in the exact cadence as before as if he's practiced saying it in the mirror. Things moved quite fast. After all, I think we had to be like around 11 years old? 

I looked down at the neon galaxy stars and purple planets of the carpeted arcade floor as Olive's feet were lifted off of it. I could feel the callused fingers against the moist skin of Olive's cheek.

I wasn't the one receiving the blows but I cried myself to sleep that night.






:: NarrativeIllness1 {"position":"775,1300","size":"100,100"}
I remember when I came down with the illness. When I mean "came down" more like I finally recognized it. I was bedridden for days riding the tide before I could truly gain the acceptance that I was sick as a fucker. 

I could barely move from my bed and I felt like I was swimming in my sheets. I've never had so much sweat come out of my pores and my hair was stuck to my skin. The ringlets that my family always gawked at as being the generational genetic treasure were becoming matted and fuzzed up like caterpillers. 

Honestly, I wish I died that day. It turned out though, I was just really damaged by the heat and I would later come to find out I'm a little more neurally fucked than I thought. [[>>->NarrativeIlness2]]


:: NarrativeIllness3 {"position":"1025,1300","size":"100,100"}

:: NarrativeIlness2 {"position":"900,1300","size":"100,100"}
I was knocked down and slapped silly by a flu and what I would later come to find out was POTS or Postural Orthostatic Tachycardia Syndrome. I had faded in and out, could barely get out of bed, and watched as the sun tinged my legs from the blinds and the moonlight awashed me overnight.

My mind was in a haze of agonizing dreams the whole time: arguments with my dad, arguments with Oliver, weird sex dreams with Oliver, and then that coach screaming at me. There was no way for me to stabilize my thoughts either. If I got up, it was like someone forced me down with one big push. My hands gripped the blankets and if I turned my world swayed to left and the right. 

Oliver finally came in to check in on me. He was gone at his parents and he didn't get a chance to off load the continued trauma tha night. I was seizing and probably would've been seized by the Gods if he didn't come back.

All I saw was Mary, the Black one in particular. She doted down and her brown eyes were so comforting, so warm. It was so rude to be waken by a shot in my ass. [[>>->NarrativeIllness3]]

