:: BlogPostThatNight1 {"position":"1375,150","size":"100,100"}
I don't want to make this too damn obvious but I don't know. I'm getting cold feet, it's like I'm getting married to the guy but I'm not. I'm 30 years old and trying to run away with a guy like I'm some 18 yr old girl running away with a suspicious guy. 

I'm leaving all my stuff here except my laptop and burner phone. Anything I need I can just buy it again. My mom and dad don't hear shit so I can run and they will think there wasn't a single sound. The old Dell laptop has missing keys and I don't care about it anymore. I don't even care if there's anything on it because it's not like my parents know how to use the laptop anyway.

When I get outside, with my bookbag all bulky like those Mainland Chinese kids on the train to Queens, for some reason the cool air and the darkness reminds me of those summer vacation days out in upstate New York.

When we would leave the hotel so early in the morning, you still think its night time. But the sky was navy blue and the sun was peeking from the envelope of darkness. The summer air would feel cool yet still. The world itself would feel like it still hasn't gotten up. My head would ache and my knees cracked. I would walk to the car and see the figure of my Dad's broad back in the front seat. His shoulders looked so big and square during that time. I would get into the car and he would always ask in this calm voice that was always unlike him and it would send me shivers because he would ask "Are you okay?"

The shivers weren't fear though. It was an ache for more of that voice he would put on. Then he would turn on the car and the radio would play the news. Now, I sit in the car with Mason and he doesn't say a single word. 


